NNAAMMEE
     units - measurement conversion

SSYYNNOOPPSSIISS
     uunniittss [-uu]

DDEESSCCRRIIPPTTIIOONN
     uunniittss is an interactive program that computes the conversion
     factor between two units of the same dimension.  It prints
     the prompt YYoouu hhaavvee: and reads the quantity you wish to con-
     vert from, then prints YYoouu wwaanntt: and reads the quantity you
     wish to convert to.  If the two are conformable (the same
     dimension), it prints the multiplicative factor to convert
     the first quantity into the second, and its reciprocal;
     otherwise it prints CCoonnffoorrmmaabbiilliittyy followed by each quantity
     broken down into its fundamental units, and prompts again.
     uunniittss loops asking for pairs of quantities until it reaches
     end of file on the standard input.

     A quantity is a number (default 1, if omitted) followed by a
     unit expression (default dimensionless, if omitted).  A unit
     expression is built from named units, optionally scaled by a
     metric prefix (such as kkiilloo or mmiillllii), raised to a power
     with a trailing +nn or -nn, and combined with / for division
     and adjacent units for multiplication; the words ppeerr
     (divide), ssqquuaarree (power 2), and ccuubbiicc (power 3) may also be
     used.

     -uu   Read the ASCII units table and rewrite the binary units
          file, then exit without prompting for any conversion.

FFIILLEESS
          /uussrr/lliibb/uunniittss  table of known units, in ASCII
          /uussrr/lliibb/bbiinnuunniittssthe same table, precompiled to binary

DDIIAAGGNNOOSSTTIICCSS
     uunniittss prints RReebbuuiillddiinngg /uussrr/lliibb/bbiinnuunniittss ffrroomm
     /uussrr/lliibb/uunniittss ...  and regenerates the binary table when-
     ever /uussrr/lliibb/uunniittss is newer than /uussrr/lliibb/bbiinnuunniittss or the
     latter is missing or unreadable; this can take a while.  It
     prints UUnnrreeccooggnniisseedd uunniitt followed by the offending name for
     a word it cannot match against any known unit, and CCoonnffoorr-
     mmaabbiilliittyy for a pair of quantities that do not have the same
     dimension.

NNOOTTEESS
     uunniittss is installed set-user-id to bbiinn so that it can write
     the shared binary table /uussrr/lliibb/bbiinnuunniittss the first time it
     is regenerated; it drops this privilege (by calling
     sseettuuiidd()) before doing any conversion.
